1
00:00:03,850 --> 00:00:06,685
Welcome to the Pre Sales Agent Framework.

2
00:00:06,685 --> 00:00:20,171
It turns the emails, call transcripts and tender documents you get from a customer into confirmed requirements, clarification questions, specialist assessments and a traceable, reviewed estimate.

3
00:00:20,171 --> 00:00:29,299
In this tour we follow one real opportunity from start to finish: Larkspur Mutual, an insurer replacing its mainframe claims system.

4
00:00:30,399 --> 00:00:35,598
The sidebar takes you to your Inbox, Opportunities, Knowledge and Admin.

5
00:00:35,598 --> 00:00:44,842
Press Control K anywhere to open the command palette: jump to any page, or create a new opportunity, without touching the mouse.

6
00:00:45,942 --> 00:00:51,292
Before the first bid, an administrator prepares the knowledge the agents rely on.

7
00:00:51,292 --> 00:00:57,963
Knowledge Sources are your own delivery guides and playbooks, tagged by product and integration type.

8
00:00:57,963 --> 00:01:02,521
Here, an insurance claims migration playbook is registered and ready.

9
00:01:03,621 --> 00:01:08,869
Checklists hold the questions you must always ask for a type of integration.

10
00:01:08,869 --> 00:01:16,810
Mandatory items become gaps automatically whenever that integration is in scope, so nothing important is forgotten.

11
00:01:17,910 --> 00:01:28,498
The Coverage matrix shows, for every product and integration type, whether you have documentation and checklists, so you can see where gap detection may be weak.

12
00:01:29,598 --> 00:01:33,537
And the Knowledge Graph draws the same picture as a map.

13
00:01:33,537 --> 00:01:41,626
Solid lines are documented links, dashed lines show missing coverage, and red rings flag stale or missing material.

14
00:01:42,726 --> 00:01:45,547
To start a bid, choose New Opportunity.

15
00:01:45,547 --> 00:01:50,249
You can type the customer, title, products and industry yourself.

16
00:01:51,349 --> 00:01:56,489
Or choose Import from file and drop in the customer's invitation email.

17
00:01:56,489 --> 00:02:05,176
The Opportunity Intake Agent reads it and fills in the fields, each one marked From file with the sentence it came from.

18
00:02:05,176 --> 00:02:08,506
Check them, set the proposal date, and create.

19
00:02:08,506 --> 00:02:11,040
The file becomes your first source.

20
00:02:12,140 --> 00:02:14,903
Every opportunity opens on its Overview.

21
00:02:14,903 --> 00:02:21,120
The tiles show confirmed requirements, open gaps, open conflicts and the current estimate.

22
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:31,413
The submission pipeline tracks each stage from sources added to baseline, and Needs you lists the items waiting for your decision, most severe first.

23
00:02:32,513 --> 00:02:40,580
Further down you'll find the submission blockers, recent activity, and the latest agent decision with its reasoning.

24
00:02:40,580 --> 00:02:45,934
For Larkspur, all eight stages are complete and version four is the baseline.

25
00:02:47,034 --> 00:02:56,741
On the Sources tab, drop in everything the customer sent: emails, Teams transcripts, Word and PDF documents, notes, or pasted text.

26
00:02:56,741 --> 00:03:06,818
Larkspur has eleven sources, including an RFP schedule, an IT email about the mainframe and payments, and two recorded customer answers.

27
00:03:06,818 --> 00:03:10,300
Every source is stored unchanged and versioned.

28
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:13,962
Select a source to open the Inspector.

29
00:03:13,962 --> 00:03:21,245
You'll see who added it and when, download the original, and read the extracted text the agents worked from.

30
00:03:22,345 --> 00:03:33,578
The Intake Agent extracts requirements from every source and groups them by category: functional, integration, data, security, non-functional and commercial.

31
00:03:33,578 --> 00:03:39,659
Each requirement carries evidence chips that point to the exact sources it came from.

32
00:03:39,659 --> 00:03:42,593
Larkspur has eighty-seven, all confirmed.

33
00:03:43,693 --> 00:03:49,014
Open a requirement to see the quoted passage highlighted in its source.

34
00:03:49,014 --> 00:03:53,735
From here you can edit, split, merge, reclassify or confirm it.

35
00:03:53,735 --> 00:04:02,429
Confirmed requirements are locked; if a later email changes one, you see it as a pending change to accept or reject.

36
00:04:02,429 --> 00:04:08,724
Instructions hidden inside customer content are treated as content and never obeyed.

37
00:04:09,824 --> 00:04:17,888
Next, the Clarification Agent looks for what's missing, and mandatory checklist items add gaps of their own.

38
00:04:17,888 --> 00:04:33,044
Here is a second opportunity, Aldermoor Health Trust, still in progress: nine open gaps ranked by impact, each with a drafted clarification question you can edit, merge, approve, export and mark as sent.

39
00:04:34,144 --> 00:04:39,136
When the customer replies, paste the answer as a source against the question.

40
00:04:39,136 --> 00:04:43,998
The gap is marked answered, and the answer can update related requirements.

41
00:04:43,998 --> 00:04:50,026
If one answer also covers other questions, the app suggests those matches for you to confirm.

42
00:04:51,126 --> 00:04:58,082
Some things the customer simply can't know yet, like how much pre-2015 data needs correcting.

43
00:04:58,082 --> 00:05:04,888
Those are marked Unknown to the customer and converted into a contingency, priced in hours.

44
00:05:04,888 --> 00:05:09,450
Things the customer must decide or provide become conditions.

45
00:05:09,450 --> 00:05:12,442
Either way, nothing is silently dropped.

46
00:05:13,542 --> 00:05:15,583
Now start the assessment run.

47
00:05:15,583 --> 00:05:28,248
Specialist agents work in parallel: Engineering for feasibility and per-integration effort, the PM Agent for phases and dependencies, and the Security Agent for mandatory controls.

48
00:05:28,248 --> 00:05:36,762
Then the Critic checks their coverage and timelines, and the Red Team argues that integrations are harder than they look.

49
00:05:37,862 --> 00:05:47,878
Each agent returns a verdict, such as proceed with conditions, with a confidence level, the effort behind it, and the requirements it relied on.

50
00:05:47,878 --> 00:05:53,512
If you disagree, raise a Challenge with new information and the agent reassesses.

51
00:05:54,612 --> 00:05:58,271
All findings land in one table, ranked by severity.

52
00:05:58,271 --> 00:06:05,804
Critical findings block submission until someone resolves them, or overrides them with a recorded reason.

53
00:06:06,904 --> 00:06:19,438
The Conflict Agent compares sources and assessments, and flags contradictions: different dates, different volumes, or one agent sizing a requirement the other skipped.

54
00:06:19,438 --> 00:06:22,740
Pick a position, give a reason, and resolve.

55
00:06:23,840 --> 00:06:31,131
For Larkspur, all thirty-eight conflicts are resolved, and each resolution records who decided and why.

56
00:06:32,231 --> 00:06:36,371
The Estimating Agent drafts the estimate from the assessments.

57
00:06:36,371 --> 00:06:44,584
Every line covers named requirements, with the role mix and effort hours, and you can edit any line in place with a reason.

58
00:06:45,684 --> 00:06:49,354
Submit stays locked while anything is unfinished.

59
00:06:49,354 --> 00:07:00,963
The blockers panel lists exactly what's missing: open gaps, assumptions not yet accepted, open conflicts and critical findings, each with a link to fix it.

60
00:07:02,063 --> 00:07:06,395
Larkspur's estimate is twelve thousand and seventy-two hours.

61
00:07:06,395 --> 00:07:11,934
The version lifecycle runs from draft, to in review, to approved, to baseline.

62
00:07:11,934 --> 00:07:19,106
A review request was sent to a named engineering reviewer, and their approval is recorded right here.

63
00:07:20,206 --> 00:07:30,423
The Assumptions Register lists every condition the estimate depends on, each linked back to the gap it came from, and each accepted by a named person.

64
00:07:31,523 --> 00:07:35,301
Contingencies are shown separately with their hours.

65
00:07:35,301 --> 00:07:46,198
Larkspur carries one thousand one hundred and forty hours of contingency, for unknowns like undocumented status codes and late regulator requirements.

66
00:07:47,298 --> 00:07:49,677
Every change creates a new version.

67
00:07:49,677 --> 00:07:58,444
Diff against any earlier version to see which lines and assumptions changed, were added or were removed, and how the total moved.

68
00:07:59,544 --> 00:08:03,816
All versions keeps the full history, with the baseline first.

69
00:08:04,916 --> 00:08:14,668
And Export produces the estimate, the assumptions register and the clarification questions as Excel or Word, ready for the proposal.

70
00:08:15,768 --> 00:08:18,997
Reviewers and owners are notified in the Inbox.

71
00:08:18,997 --> 00:08:27,378
Review requests and decisions arrive here, so a reviewer can open the estimate, approve it, or send it back with comments.

72
00:08:28,478 --> 00:08:35,852
Once the project is delivered, record actual hours against each estimate line, with a variance cause.

73
00:08:35,852 --> 00:08:42,642
Overruns can name the assumption that failed, which feeds the estimate-versus-actual reports.

74
00:08:43,742 --> 00:08:48,755
To import actuals, download the template, fill it in, and upload it.

75
00:08:48,755 --> 00:08:53,030
You see a preview, and nothing is saved until you confirm.

76
00:08:54,130 --> 00:09:00,912
And the Trace tab is the append-only audit log of every action, by people and agents alike.

77
00:09:00,912 --> 00:09:06,576
Filter by subject, actor or event to follow any number back to its evidence.

78
00:09:07,676 --> 00:09:11,149
Administrators manage the platform under Admin.

79
00:09:11,149 --> 00:09:22,676
Users and roles shows each person's roles, which are managed in Auth0: presales engineer, delivery manager, engineering reviewer and platform administrator.

80
00:09:23,776 --> 00:09:32,135
The Catalogue defines the integration types and work packages that checklists, assessments and estimate lines share.

81
00:09:33,235 --> 00:09:38,917
The Agent Registry shows every agent, its version, model and tool permissions.

82
00:09:38,917 --> 00:09:43,870
Any tool call an agent isn't allowed to make is blocked and audited.

83
00:09:44,970 --> 00:09:56,951
And Evals runs the agents against reference sets, checking release bars like extraction recall, citation validity and gap recall before a new configuration is accepted.

84
00:09:58,051 --> 00:10:07,200
In Settings, choose a light, dark or system theme, a comfortable or compact density, and turn on single-key shortcuts.

85
00:10:08,300 --> 00:10:21,229
That's the full journey: from a customer's first email, to evidence-backed requirements, answered questions, specialist assessments, and a reviewed, baselined estimate you can trace and measure.

86
00:10:21,229 --> 00:10:24,428
Open the user guide for every feature in detail.

87
00:10:24,428 --> 00:10:25,761
Thanks for watching.
